Backport of zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr PR #122444 ("drivers: adc: ads1x1x:
support several channels") onto the ZMK Zephyr 4.1 fork (v4.1.0+zmk-fixes).

The ADS1015 and ADS1115 have one converter behind a four-input multiplexer,
but the driver only accepted channel 0. With this patch each channel keeps its
own input, gain and data rate, and a sequence converts its channels one after
the other, lowest channel first, so a driver such as the pointing stick can
read two axes from one chip.

The 4.1 fork differs from Zephyr main in two small places before the PR, and
the backport keeps both: the input multiplexer block is not wrapped in
ADC_ADS1X1X_CONFIGURABLE_INPUTS, and chips without a multiplexer still check
that the input pair is differential 0 and 1. The fork's ADS Kconfig already
selects ADC_CONFIGURABLE_INPUTS.
Drop this patch once ZMK moves to a Zephyr release that contains the PR.

